    "§23.3 step 6",
    "§6.4",
    "§12.2 step 13s"
  ],
  "notes": "Python: tests/tasks/test_failed_worker_turn.py::test_a_worker_turn_failed_after_a_round_keeps_its_end; core/mixins/_child_execution.py _turn_failure (TaskTurnFailedError: the end and the narration the child room's record holds), tasks/models.py finished_task_fields. worker runs inline on the trace, writer inline with email shared, seeker in the background on the trace, finder in the background with email shared. Python's test fails with a ProviderError whose text leads with its provider and status (mock (400): upstream 400, providers/ai/base.py ProviderError.__str__); a scripted model names no provider, so the error is its message. The provider refuses the second generation (an error it does not retry, a ProviderError as in Python's test), after the tool round: the turn's end is error (channels/_ai_streaming.py _stream_generation).",
